stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Created: User action occurs

    Created --> Buffered: Add to memory buffer
    Buffered --> Persisted: Periodic flush (5s)<br/>or buffer full (1000)

    Persisted --> Indexed: Database INSERT complete
    Indexed --> Cached: Store counters in Redis
    Cached --> Published: Emit to Event Bus

    Published --> Analyzed: Real-time stream consumers
    Published --> Aggregated: Hourly/daily rollups

    state "Activity States" as states {
        Analyzed --> Active: Within retention period
        Active --> Aging: Approaching anonymization
    }

    state "Privacy Lifecycle" as privacy {
        Aging --> Anonymized: After anonymizeAfterDays
        Anonymized --> Archived: PII removed
        Archived --> Deleted: After deleteAfterDays
    }

    state "Analytics Processing" as analytics {
        Aggregated --> HourlyRollup
        Aggregated --> DailyRollup
        Aggregated --> WeeklyRollup
        Aggregated --> MonthlyRollup

        HourlyRollup --> StatisticsCache
        DailyRollup --> StatisticsCache
        WeeklyRollup --> StatisticsCache
        MonthlyRollup --> StatisticsCache
    }

    state "Security Monitoring" as security {
        Analyzed --> RateLimitCheck
        RateLimitCheck --> PatternDetection
        PatternDetection --> SuspiciousActivity: Threshold exceeded
        SuspiciousActivity --> SecurityAlert
        SecurityAlert --> AuditLog
    }

    Deleted --> [*]

    note right of Created
        Activity event created with:
        - userId
        - type (ActivityType enum)
        - metadata (IP, device, etc)
        - timestamp
    end note

    note right of Buffered
        High-throughput optimization:
        - In-memory buffer (1000 items)
        - Batch INSERT reduces DB load
        - Non-blocking for API response
    end note

    note right of Anonymized
        GDPR Compliance:
        - Remove PII (IP, user agent)
        - Keep aggregated statistics
        - Maintain data utility
    end note

    note right of SecurityAlert
        Fraud Detection Triggers:
        - Rapid requests (>100/min)
        - Failed logins (>5/15min)
        - Multiple locations
        - Unusual times (2am-5am)
    end note
